// The sprites of the Sci-Fi skin, cut out of UI Pack Sci-Fi by Kenney (kenney.nl/assets/ui-pack-sci-fi, CC0) by
// Art/make_ui_packs.py, which is where to change anything in here, this file is written by it. This is the skin
// that isn't pixel art. It is the pack at its double size, flat shapes with round corners, and the skin draws it
// at half (art_scale 0.5) and smoothed, so it has four of its own pixels for every one of a 1600 by 900 screen and
// stays sharp on a screen of twice that or with the UI scaled up. The pack is a folder of PNGs per colour, the same
// pieces in each, and those colours are the themes here, a layer of art.aseprite each.
//
// The names are the ones the components and the layouts ask for, which are Dead Revolver's, so a layout written
// for that skin comes up in this one. The pack has no button under the pointer or held down, those are the plain
// one made a little lighter and a little darker. Where a face isn't the colour the skin writes on (the solid
// bars are written on in white, the glass in slate) the sprite says so itself with a text_color.

